From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armada <armada@thucommix.dev>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] msm: report GPU memory and RAM usage

msm shares the system RAM with the CPU, so drm-memory-vram never exists
and the VRAM row always read 0.0. Since Linux 6.5 the DRM fdinfo
interface exposes drm-resident-memory, so use that for the VRAM row and
PVRAM on msm_dpu. The value is per-client (the focused game), which is
the only GPU-memory counter the driver exposes.

Show the RAM usage percentage next to the used amount instead of a
smaller "/total" appended to it, which crowded the number, and move
swap to a labelled SWAP row.

Hide the VRAM memory-temp, GPU temp and memory-clock cells when no
sensor backs them. msm has no vram sensor or memory clock, and these
handhelds have no RAM spd5118, so those cells rendered a constant
0 degC / 0 MHz.

Pick gpuss_0_thermal deterministically for the GPU temperature instead
of whichever hwmon device containing "gpu" is enumerated first, and
fall back to the gpuss-* thermal zones when no GPU hwmon exists.
---
 src/gpu_fdinfo.cpp   | 108 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/gpu_fdinfo.h     |  10 ++++-
 src/hud_elements.cpp |  42 +++++++++++++++-----
 src/memory.cpp       |   8 +++-
 4 files changed, 155 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)
